module

public import MathFin.Pricing.FTAP.DensityPasting
public import MathFin.Pricing.FTAP.NoArbitrageLocal

/-!
# The Dalang–Morton–Willinger theorem for several assets, reduced to its conditional one-period core

The multi-period fundamental theorem of asset pricing on a general probability space with `d`
assets (`F = EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)`) and a finite horizon: no arbitrage if and only if there is
an equivalent martingale measure. The standard proof (Föllmer–Schied, *Stochastic Finance*, §5.2;
Rogers 1994; Kabanov–Stricker 2001) has three steps. This file assembles the first two with the
third isolated as one precisely stated hypothesis.

1. **Reduction** (`NoArbitrageLocal.lean`): multi-period no arbitrage is equivalent to no
   arbitrage in each one-period market conditional on `𝓕 t` (`noArbitrage_iff_noArbitrageLocal`),
   and conditional no arbitrage passes to equivalent measures
   (`NoArbitrageAt.of_absolutelyContinuous`).
2. **Pasting** (`DensityPasting.lean`): one-period densities `Z t ∈ [0, 1]`, a.s. positive, fair
   against every bounded `𝓕 t`-measurable position, chosen backward under the measure already
   weighted by the later periods, and normalised once at the end, give an equivalent martingale
   measure (`exists_isEMM_of_onePeriodDensities`).
3. **The conditional one-period FTAP** (not proved here): conditional no arbitrage at period `t`
   produces such a density under every finite measure `ν ≤ P` equivalent to `P`
   (`ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP`). This is the measurable-selection core of the theorem: the
   one-period theorem (`OnePeriodVector.ftap_one_period_vector`) carried out conditionally on a
   non-trivial `𝓕 t`, and it is the hypothesis, not a theorem, for `d > 1`. For `d = 1` it is
   `OneAsset.exists_onePeriodDensity` (`OneAssetDMW.lean`).

The one-period densities are unnormalised on purpose. A *normalised* conditional density, bounded
with `E[Z | 𝓕 t] = 1`, can fail to exist for an arbitrage-free market (take `𝓕 t` generated by a
uniform `u` and `ΔS = ±1` with `P (ΔS = 1 | u) = u`: it would equal `1 / (2u)` on `{ΔS = 1}`),
whereas the weights in `[0, 1]` always do for one asset.

So what is proved is: **assuming** the conditional one-period FTAP, no arbitrage is equivalent to
the existence of an equivalent martingale measure. The forward direction (an equivalent martingale
measure precludes arbitrage) is `IsEMM.noArbitrage` and needs no hypothesis. For one real asset the
theorem is proved unconditionally in `OneAssetDMW.lean` (`OneAsset.noArbitrage_iff_exists_isEMM`).
The several-asset case on a general space remains open in this library (issue #313): the
hypothesis below is its missing step.

## Main definitions

* `ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP`: conditional no arbitrage at each period, under each finite measure
  equivalent to `P` and below it, yields a one-period density (`IsOnePeriodDensity`).

## Main results

* `exists_isEMM_of_noArbitrage_of_conditionalFTAP`: given `ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP`, no
  arbitrage gives an equivalent martingale measure.
* `noArbitrage_iff_exists_isEMM`: given `ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP`, no arbitrage is equivalent
  to the existence of an equivalent martingale measure.

## References

* [H. Föllmer and A. Schied, *Stochastic Finance: An Introduction in Discrete Time*][FollmerSchied],
  §5.2

## Tags

fundamental theorem of asset pricing, Dalang–Morton–Willinger, equivalent martingale measure,
no arbitrage, general probability space, conditional one-period market, JEL G13, MSC 91G20,
MSC 60G42
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace MathFin

open MeasureTheory

variable {Ω : Type*} {m0 : MeasurableSpace Ω} {d : ℕ}
  {𝓕 : Filtration ℕ m0} {P : Measure Ω} {S : ℕ → Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)}

/-- **The conditional one-period FTAP** for the price `S` up to the horizon `T`, as a hypothesis:
for every period `t < T` and every finite measure `ν ≤ P` equivalent to `P`, no arbitrage in the
conditional one-period market of `t` under `ν` (`NoArbitrageAt`) yields a one-period density under
`ν` (`IsOnePeriodDensity`: an `𝓕 (t+1)`-measurable weight in `[0, 1]`, a.s. positive, making the
increment fair against every bounded `𝓕 t`-measurable position). It is **not proved** in this
library for `d > 1`: it is the measurable-selection core of the Dalang–Morton–Willinger theorem,
the conditional version of `OnePeriodVector.ftap_one_period_vector`. The unconditional one-asset
case is `OneAsset.exists_onePeriodDensity`. -/
def ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP (𝓕 : Filtration ℕ m0) (P : Measure Ω)
    (S : ℕ → Ω → EuclideanSpace ℝ (Fin d)) (T : ℕ) : Prop :=
  ∀ t < T, ∀ ν : Measure Ω, IsFiniteMeasure ν → ν ≤ P → P ≪ ν → NoArbitrageAt 𝓕 ν S t →
    ∃ Z, IsOnePeriodDensity 𝓕 ν S t Z

variable [IsProbabilityMeasure P] {T : ℕ}

/-- **Dalang–Morton–Willinger, assuming the conditional one-period FTAP**: for an adapted
integrable price, if the conditional one-period FTAP holds (`ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP`) then no
arbitrage gives an equivalent martingale measure. The reduction
`noArbitrageLocal_of_noArbitrage` turns multi-period no arbitrage into conditional no arbitrage in
each period, which passes to every equivalent measure, the hypothesis produces a density per
period, and the densities paste (`exists_isEMM_of_onePeriodDensities`). -/
theorem exists_isEMM_of_noArbitrage_of_conditionalFTAP
    (hS : ∀ t ≤ T, StronglyMeasurable[𝓕 t] (S t))
    (hint : ∀ t ≤ T, Integrable (S t) P) (hcond : ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP 𝓕 P S T)
    (hNA : NoArbitrage 𝓕 P S T) : ∃ Q, IsEMM 𝓕 P S T Q :=
  exists_isEMM_of_onePeriodDensities hS hint fun t ht ν hν hνP hPν ↦
    hcond t ht ν hν hνP hPν
      ((noArbitrageLocal_of_noArbitrage hNA t ht).of_absolutelyContinuous
        (Measure.absolutelyContinuous_of_le hνP) hPν)

/-- **Dalang–Morton–Willinger, assuming the conditional one-period FTAP**: for an adapted
integrable price, if `ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP` holds then no arbitrage is equivalent to the
existence of an equivalent martingale measure. The converse is `IsEMM.noArbitrage`. -/
theorem noArbitrage_iff_exists_isEMM (hS : ∀ t ≤ T, StronglyMeasurable[𝓕 t] (S t))
    (hint : ∀ t ≤ T, Integrable (S t) P) (hcond : ConditionalOnePeriodFTAP 𝓕 P S T) :
    NoArbitrage 𝓕 P S T ↔ ∃ Q, IsEMM 𝓕 P S T Q :=
  ⟨exists_isEMM_of_noArbitrage_of_conditionalFTAP hS hint hcond, fun ⟨_, hQ⟩ ↦ hQ.noArbitrage⟩

end MathFin
